-- Deneb Dual-Line Variance Chart — DAX measures
--
-- Apart from [DualLine Row Count] below, these measures are for OTHER visuals on the report page (KPI cards, a
-- Clustered bar/column chart used as the cross-highlight source in บทที่ 8,
-- etc.) — NOT for the Dual-Line Variance Chart itself. The chart binds
-- directly to the DualLine_PlotData table built by Power Query
-- (specs/DualLine_PlotData_PowerQuery.pq); Actual/Reference there are plain
-- Columns already at the correct grain, not Measures.
--
-- Table: DualLineVariance_Workshop_Data (the raw input table, before
-- Power Query builds DualLine_PlotData from it)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Table: DualLine_PlotData (the Power Query table the chart binds to)
--
-- REQUIRED in the Deneb Values well (Phase 2 evidence T23, 24 Sep 2026):
-- Actual/Reference are bound as Sum (implicit measures) so Deneb can expose
-- Actual__highlight / __highlightStatus for cross-highlight. Boundary/Crossing
-- rows have Actual/Reference = Blank, and Power BI drops rows whose measures are
-- all Blank -> the dataset shrank from 52 to 12 rows and the variance area
-- disappeared. This measure is never Blank, so every row is kept. The spec does
-- not read it. See PHASE1_DESIGN_PLAN.md section 2.1.1.
DualLine Row Count =
COUNTROWS ( DualLine_PlotData )

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Table: DualLineVariance_Workshop_Data (measures for other visuals)

Total Actual =
SUM ( DualLineVariance_Workshop_Data[Actual] )

Total Reference =
SUM ( DualLineVariance_Workshop_Data[Reference] )

Variance =
[Total Actual] - [Total Reference]

Variance % =
DIVIDE ( [Variance], [Total Reference] )

-- Achievement % follows the Business_Type direction, not a hardcoded "higher is better".
-- Business_Type_Source lives on DualLineVariance_Settings (single row) — see
-- PHASE1_DESIGN_PLAN.md section 3. This measure is illustrative only; the
-- Dual-Line Variance Chart itself reads Business_Type from DualLine_PlotData,
-- not from this measure.
Achievement % =
VAR BusinessType = SELECTEDVALUE ( DualLineVariance_Settings[Business_Type_Source], "Higher is Good" )
VAR RawRatio = DIVIDE ( [Total Actual], [Total Reference] )
RETURN
    IF ( BusinessType = "Lower is Good", DIVIDE ( [Total Reference], [Total Actual] ), RawRatio )
